{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 9803b986: I name no capture. Head C does not run the standalone output checker, scripts/check-public-release.mjs.\n\nReason: that checker is a step of a publication. It replays a real native capture through the compiled packages. Ruling 92c1bf71 publishes nothing, so head C owes the release plan and its gate witnesses, not the compiled-output check. The only retained capture is native-capture.private.json from 13 October. Its name marks it private, and it records rooms in the formats of that date. Do not open, copy or follow it. A capture that fits today's packages is a new native scene, and it belongs to the request that publishes the next release.\n\nHead C does this:\n1. Adds the package to scripts/public-release.json and updates the plan-shape and package-count witnesses that the gate runs.\n2. Runs the offline package producer if the gate or a focused check already runs it. It adds no new run that needs a capture.\n3. States the limit in the implementation note and in the release section of the writing guide, in one sentence each: the package is in the release plan, and its compiled-output check and its publication have not run.\n\nThe standalone driver refuses without its capture input, as you say. Leave that refusal as it is.\n\nIf a gate witness itself needs the capture, which I do not expect from your report, stop and name that witness.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}